{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1474210-reign-of-the-orichalcum-rule-a-new-ex3-campaign-mad-ramblings","id":1474210,"title":"Reign of the Orichalcum rule: a new Ex3 campaign mad ramblings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-08T10:37:05-08:00","id":1474210,"title":"Reign of the Orichalcum rule: a new Ex3 campaign mad ramblings","content":"So 3-4 years after my Dark Ages Vampire campaign died out (narrated here), my group has finally grown restless and are craving for a new game. As in really ravenous. So... well, before playing my Vampire game, we were playing Exalted 1st-2nd edition (but me as a player). That game lasted for some time (and I think I also have posted around my Dawn caste character's art, and then my Eclipse caste later character, when the other half retired) but basically the guy directing it got tired (and that's why I had to organized the Dark Ages stuff).<br /> <br /> Well, the thing is here I am. And I decided to take my same approach I had for vampire. Basically: have in mind that the target destination had to basically appear the same as it is in the premise of the games... but then going to the very creation of the universe, and work up with my own internal logic and tastes how things actually work, and how key events happened. Which means nothing is at all like in canon, but at a base level appearance. To be honest, one of the reasons I can't find myself to work within the stablished canon is the fact it hardly ever makes sense to me. Which... well, it's not only in rpg settings that are 'wide' enough, but basically in any fandom that has not been written by a single author. For instance... Star Wars hardly makes sense at all (even having in mind only the first trilogy, but much much less if you even try to push in the prequels... and... well, the less said about the sequels, the better). But for example Wheel of Time, basically a single epic story by the same author (yes, I know Sanderson finished it, but still it was following notes) or, say, Lord of the Rings I would still make sense of it. But things like Vampire, or Exalted... no way. It just clashes way too much together. So the first thought I have is... well, we start with the Chaos. And some part of the Chaos... well, it kind of takes conscience of itself. So what happens from there so we can end up with The Realm, the exalted, the gods, etc.<br /> <br /> Well, one thing that is a problem for me is the 'oriental' tradition. It's hard for me to work in that context, when it's something that... well, it's not a matter of cultural appropiation, I think that would be an exaggeration. But yet there are some eastern religious concepts from hinduism to daoism and confuncianism imbedded in the mythos of exalted that... can't work for me. So when I go to the start of things, where do I go? well, to the greek mythos, of course. With a little touch of Tolkien, maybe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> So what I end having is basically something like Hesiod's Theogony generations of gods. Chaos thinks, for the first time, an odd, unexpected part of the all and nothing that is. And since it thinks, it can not be himself, and since it's not himself it's something else, and that something else is the heaven and earth. Uranus and Gaia, in the mythos. Mardukh and... well. It's still Gaia here. And suddenly there's a core of reality, that is still a juvenile Gaia, forming, starting to form what herself truly is and there's a heaven around her, protecting her. Mardukh, Heaven but in a way pure order, as in opposition of chaos and change, a shroud for Gaia. Cold order against the raw chaos, a barrier that is himself and is what he does. Hard rules. The very concept of rigidity, of strict rules. In a way of tyranny, but when around you there's only a chaos that would desintegrate you, destroy you, not out of malice but by its very nature, tyranny is rather a refuge and a protection.<br /> <br /> But as they evolve, as they combine, heaven and earth meet and combine, and from pieces of chaos they can absorb and integrate, they procreate. And there we would have what would be our generation of 'titans'. And what concept, what children do they stablish... well, Malfeas as the concept of rulership, of tamed order within creation. Order that can direct, that can harbor change. Of the very concept of Time and passage, the framework so things can happen and that's Adrian. And finally there's the rulership itself, but there are the Rules that are a thing unto themselves, and taht concept is Cecelyne. And with those children, Earth and heaven changed, and mixed. But that first heaven was cold and unmoving. And when Rulership and Earth met/mate the concept of directed Creation comes, and as a concept is a thing and a new concept in itself, and thus we have Authochton. And when Time and Earth came, Earth become fluid like the river of time and thus the very concept of the endless ocean appeared, wrapping against Gaia, the great Kimberly.<br /> <br /> But finally Gaia met the rules. And made rules for itself. And in a way that was other shroud, other... sky. And it was dark and endless, not cold and unmoving. And when Mardukh looked against Gaia and saw she was wrapped into a Dragon that appeared to be made of Shadow, he felt aggraviated. He felt betrayed. Gaia was his mate in and against chaos. Wasn't his essence all she needed to be in the midst of the endless Chaos. And he extended himself, and he invaded all that was and could be. And he froze the endless sea, and the river of time. He made the endless shadow cold and merciless. And the three and three and one saw they could not be what they could be with such constrain. And they turned against Mardukh. And they ripped his insides, his very essence, and from him made Yu-Shan, the perfect heaven, over Gaia. And the other 6 could inhabit and overview over Gaia and see how they could enhance their mother and sister and mate.<br /> <br /> And that was the first usurpation. The concept of Mardukh is mentioned in the books and the background, but mostly passed over, as a vague concept that there was a previous ruler and now it was not remembered. And that made me think of the dethronement of Uranos in the Greek Mythos... And that combined with the fact that... unless I have missed something Yu-Shan is just... made and that's it. We have Gaia that is the primordial herself. We have Hell that is Malfeas. And so on. But... Yu-Shan is not quite gaia and is right there. So what if Yu-Shan was actually a 'frozen dead' Mardukh? And that's why molded by the other primordials, Yu-Shan is such an embodiment of perfection, and yet of rigidity.<br /> <br /> Of course, having Yu-Shan made of the first Tyrant would have... interesting consequences for the future.<br /> <br /> So this is my little start for my own... eh... Exalted Theogony. I hope it did not sound as unbearably pretentious and silly as I fear it sounds, but it was fun trying to reason things from the beggining. And yeah, I know there are a lot more of primordials, but you will see how they get here.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed the read! I hope to be coming and continuing this for some time until we reach to the vanishing of the Empress but for today I have written too much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3320-cathakjordi","name":"CathakJordi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}